e conscious subject must stand ontologically outside the material medium used to describe it. Principal limitation: Being painted with paint does not straightforwardly entail being constituted by paint, and the shifting roles of painter, portrait, subject, and medium leave the intended correspondence unstable. Live burden: Jump needs a nonmetaphorical reason to believe consciousness can be constituted by matter, especially after Kastrup distinguishes quantitative structure from qualitative experience, rather than relying upon an altered picture."}}
